      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 109,
      "outputTokens": 856,
      "costUsd": 0.0077585,
      "pronunciationText": "Acceleration is how fast the velocity changes. So it's the derivative of velocity, which is the second derivative of displacement. We write it as d two x by d t squared, or as x with two dots on top, said x double dot. Here, x double dot is six t minus eighteen, in centimetres per second, per second. It's negative before three seconds, and positive after. At two seconds the robot is at rest, but its acceleration is minus six, so it's about to start moving left."
    },
