      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 0,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 109,
      "outputTokens": 823,
      "costUsd": 0.0074615,
      "pronunciationText": "Velocity is a rate, so last video's idea works here too. Integrating velocity over an interval gives the change in displacement. From zero to six seconds, that's x of six minus x of zero, which is thirty-six centimetres. But the robot didn't just travel thirty-six centimetres. It went right twenty, back four, then right another twenty, so it covered forty-four centimetres in total. The integral gives the displacement. For the distance, add the size of each leg, between the rest times."
    },
